{"mls":"S1676056","addr":"6693 Route 305","muni":"Belfast town","town":"Belfast","county":"Allegany","zip":"14711","ll":[42.325048,-78.113231],"status":"Active","type":"Single Family","units":1,"beds":3,"baths":0,"sqft":1728.0,"year":1990,"lot":6.25,"dom":60,"price":149900,"orig":164900,"chg":"Price Change","tax":4039,"tax_mls":true,"hoa":null,"office":"Landquest Inc.","phone":"585.466.3446","hhp":false,"remarks":"This Amish built home with a barn and a pole barn is located in Belfast NY, Allegany County.\r\n\r\nThis country homestead has open views of the surrounding valley.  A covered front porch welcomes you into the home where an open living and dining area features hardwood floors and natural light.  The kitchen includes cupboard storage and countertop space.  A first-floor bedroom adds convenience, along with an enclosed porch that works well as an office or sitting area.  Upstairs, you will find an additional bedroom and an unfinished attic that offers storage or potential for more living space.  The full basement includes a wood stove and has both interior and exterior access.\r\n\r\nThe land consists of 6.25 acres and offers a yard suitable for recreation, fenced areas for horses or cattle, and a small water feature.  Several outbuildings provide added function, including a large barn with stalls, a pole barn with a small office area previously used for a sawmill or lumber business, and another shop building with a wood stove.  Electric is available at the driveway entrance.\r\n\r\nLocated just a short drive to the Town of Belfast and the Genesee River where you can enjoy canoeing, kayaking, and fishing.  This property offers potential for residential, seasonal use, or a business opportunity.  All rights convey.","facts":[["Total rooms","7"],["Full baths","0"],["Half baths","0"],["Style","Two Story"],["Stories","1"],["Building area (sq ft)","1,728"],["Heating","Wood, Gravity"],["Basement","Full"],["Foundation","Block"],["Construction","Frame, Wood Siding"],